9982 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/P 8636 0 R/S/Figure/Alt(The ten books of the Law of Fairness series are displayed in two rows, each with a distinct symbol representing its subject. Together, the books move from the central Law and its scientific investigation through questions of utopia, transition, personal life, religion, government, civic life, constitutional structure, and lasting peace.\nPrinted panel text:\nTHE TEN BOOKS OF FAIRNESS. A complete path from truth to practice.\nTop row, left to right:\nThe Law of Fairness: Explores the core question, defines key terms, and sets the ethical bounds of the series.\nThe Science of Fairness: Evaluates the Law through evidence, measurement, rival models, protocols, and falsification.\nThe Utopia of Fairness: Brings the series into a mature view of what a peaceful world could become.\nThe Transition of Fairness: Asks how a move toward utopia could unfold with care, step by step, under real limits.\nThe Life of Fairness: Brings the Law into daily life and asks what it means for how we live.\nBottom row, left to right:\nThe Religion of Fairness: Explores faith, world religions, and the optional path of Fairness.\nThe Government of Fairness: Examines civic structure and the public institutions that give it form in practice.\nThe City of Fairness: Builds a civic space for learning, service, and peace with privacy kept safe.\nThe Constitution of Fairness: Sets out the rights, rules, paths, and checks a lasting utopia would need.\nThe Peace of Fairness: Builds the base for lasting peace and a fairer future for all humanity.\nThe series moves from the deepest question about reality to the structures that make a more peaceful world.)/K[0]/Pg 48 0 R/A 9984 0 R>>
endobj

